<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aetnaeus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		Aetna. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pertaining to Ætna</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
					D. 2, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres,</span>”
				<i>the Cyclopes who forged in Mt. Ætna</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 678</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fulmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 4, 16, 21</span></i>
			: Deus, i. e. <i>Vulcan</i>, who is said to have
			had his forge in Mt. Ætna, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 2,
				420</span></i>.— <i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aetnaei</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>those
				who dwell on</i> or <i>near Mt.
			Ætna</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 22, 1</span></i>.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, pars pro toto, <i>Sicilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triumphi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					9, 196</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
